{'symbol': 'AMAT', 'date': '2022-12-14 07:30:00', 'title': "APPLIED MATERIALS BREAKTHROUGH IN ELECTRON BEAM IMAGING TECHNOLOGY ACCELERATES DEVELOPMENT OF THE WORLD'S MOST ADVANCED COMPUTER CHIPS", 'text': 'SANTA CLARA, CALIF., DEC. 14, 2022 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- APPLIED MATERIALS, INC. TODAY ANNOUNCED THE COMMERCIAL AVAILABILITY OF “COLD FIELD EMISSION” (CFE) TECHNOLOGY, A BREAKTHOUGH IN EBEAM IMAGING THAT ENABLES CUSTOMERS TO BETTER DETECT AND IMAGE NANOMETER-SCALE, BURIED DEFECTS TO SPEED THE DEVELOPMENT AND PRODUCTION OF NEXT-GENERATION GATE-ALL-AROUND (GAA) LOGIC CHIPS AS WELL AS HIGHER-DENSITY DRAM AND 3D NAND MEMORIES.'}